# direnv entrypoint — loads the flake's devShell whenever you `cd` into
# this repo so the patched Zig 0.15.2 (macOS 26 TBD fix) + msgfmt land
# on PATH automatically. No more remembering to type `nix develop`
# before `./scripts/reload.sh`.
#
# First-time setup on this machine:
#   1. `brew install direnv` (or `nix profile install nixpkgs#direnv`)
#   2. Hook direnv into your shell:
#        zsh:  add `eval "$(direnv hook zsh)"`  to ~/.zshrc
#        bash: add `eval "$(direnv hook bash)"` to ~/.bashrc
#        fish: add `direnv hook fish | source`  to ~/.config/fish/config.fish
#   3. Inside this repo, run `direnv allow` once (direnv refuses to
#      auto-load until you opt in for a given .envrc).
#
# Speed tip: install `nix-direnv` to cache the evaluated shell. Without
# it, every `cd` re-evaluates the flake (~10 s); with it, only the
# first entry pays the cost. Stock `use flake` falls back gracefully
# when nix-direnv isn't present.
if has nix_direnv_version; then
  nix_direnv_version 3.0.0
  use flake
else
  use flake
fi
